    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>House Republicans voted to formalize an impeachment inquiry into <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/candidates/joe-biden-2024/\">President Biden</a>.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Why?</b> Republicans have not said what alleged crimes they would <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/impeachment-inquiry-biden/\">try to impeach Biden for</a>, and they haven\u2019t <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/biden-impeachment-inquiry-vote-analysis/\">shown evidence</a> that he benefited financially from his son Hunter\u2019s foreign deals.",
        "<b>The vote:</b> No Democrats <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/impeachment-inquiry-vote-hunter-biden-subpoena/\">supported the move</a> yesterday. And it\u2019s unclear whether Republicans have the votes, or <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/gops-impeachment-inquiry-starts-shaky-political-ground/\">political will</a>, to impeach. (See how your representative voted <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/interactive/2023/biden-impeachment-inquiry-vote-count/\">here</a>.)",
        "<b>What else happened?</b> Hunter Biden <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/hunter-biden-defiant-appearance/\">defied a House subpoena</a> to testify behind closed doors."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "2",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>The Supreme Court will hear a case involving access to a key <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/abortion/\">abortion</a> drug.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>What drug? </b>Mifepristone, which is used in more than <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/03/15/mifepristone-fda-approval-history/\">half of U.S. abortions</a>. The court should decide by the end of June <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/abortion-drug-supreme-court-mifepristone-fda/\">whether to restrict it</a>, it announced yesterday.",
        "<b>What it means: </b>The issue of <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/pregnant-women-take-leading-role-new-legal-battles-over-abortion/\">reproductive rights</a> is returning to the high court for the first time since it <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/24/abortion-state-laws-criminalization-roe/\">overturned <i>Roe v. Wade</i></a> last year.",
        "<b>What else to know: </b>The court will hear a case that could <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/jan-6-obstruction-supreme-court-trump-rioters/\">undo hundreds of charges</a> stemming from Jan. 6, 2021 attack."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "3",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Biden met with relatives of American hostages held by <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/10/09/hamas-israel-war-explainer/\">Hamas</a>.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>What to know:</b> The president\u2019s <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/13/biden-meets-families-american-hostages/\">first in-person meeting</a> with the group lasted over two hours yesterday. At least <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/30/hamas-hostages-list-names-tracker-israel-gaza/\">eight Americans</a> remain captive <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/12/14/israel-hamas-gaza-war-news-palestine/\">in the Gaza Strip</a>.",
        "<b>What else to know:</b> A U.S. official called images of Palestinian men stripped and detained by Israeli soldiers \u201c<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/12/13/gaza-palestinian-detainee-photos-israel/?itid=lk_inline_manual_18\">deeply disturbing</a>.\u201d"
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "4",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Ohio legislators passed a ban on gender-affirming care for minors.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "ad1",
      "breakpoints": [
        "small"
      ],
      "kind": "block",
      "size": "tall",
      "adPath": "/the-seven"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>What to know:</b> The bill, <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2023/12/13/ohio-gender-affirming-care-ban-legislature/\">passed yesterday</a>, prohibits hormone therapy, puberty blockers and gender reassignment surgery. It now goes to the governor.",
        "<b>What it means: </b>Transgender youths in <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2022/10/14/anti-trans-bills/\">states with similar bans</a> who had been traveling to Ohio for care may soon need other options."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "ad",
      "breakpoints": [
        "small"
      ],
      "kind": "block",
      "size": "tall",
      "adPath": "/the-seven"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "5",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Tesla recalled more than 2 million cars over safety concerns.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Why?</b> The cars\u2019 Autopilot systems do <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/12/13/tesla-autopilot-recall/\">not have enough controls to prevent misuse</a>, U.S. safety regulators determined. (<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/12/13/tesla-recall-autopilot/\">Here\u2019s what to do</a> if your car is affected.)",
        "<b>The problem:</b> Tesla drivers are able to <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/interactive/2023/tesla-autopilot-crash-analysis/\">engage Autopilot</a> on roads where it <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/12/10/tesla-autopilot-cross-traffic/\">can\u2019t reliably operate</a>, like those with cross-traffic \u2014 with sometimes <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2023/12/10/tesla-autopilot-crash/\">deadly consequences</a>."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "ad",
      "breakpoints": [
        "large"
      ],
      "kind": "float",
      "size": "medium",
      "adPath": "/the-seven"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "6",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>The Dow Jones Industrial Average hit an all-time high.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Why?</b> The Federal Reserve <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/12/13/fed-interest-rate-decision-inflation-fomc/\">left interest rates flat </a>again yesterday \u2014 raising the possibility that they could lower them in 2024. The last rate hike came in July.",
        "<b>What it means: </b>There\u2019s fresh optimism in financial markets, spurred by a belief that the economy is cooling just enough to lower inflation <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/12/13/dow-jones-stock-market-record-high-economy-interest-rates/\">without triggering a recession</a>."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "7",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Ikea is giving away massive \u201cturkey-sized\u201d meatballs in the U.K.</b>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "imageURL": "https://arc-anglerfish-washpost-prod-washpost.s3.amazonaws.com/public/QKZGUAONUYYGKJL5KGXGB5LU6A.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 2000,
      "imageHeight": 1334,
      "image_type": "photograph",
      "widthFactor": "full-bleed",
      "fullcaption": "(Ikea UK and Ireland)",
      "blurb": "(Ikea UK and Ireland)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>What you\u2019re looking at:</b> A giant version of the Swedish furniture retailer\u2019s cult-favorite cafeteria meatballs. This one can <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/food/2023/12/13/ikea-giant-meatball-turkey-size-contest/\">feed up to 25 people</a>, the company said.",
        "<b>This isn\u2019t a joke: </b>As part of a holiday contest, Ikea is giving away 30 of the meaty orbs and 30 veggie options. (If you don\u2019t win, <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/ikeas-swedish-meatballs-cream-sauce/\">here\u2019s how to make your own regular-size meatballs</a>.)"
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "And now \u2026 <b>not into meatballs?</b> Try one of our <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/food/2023/12/13/top-20-recipes-2023/\">20 most popular recipes of 2023</a>.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<i>Jamie Ross contributed to this report.</i>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<i>Want to catch up quickly with \u201cThe 7\u201d every morning? </i><a href=\"https://wapo.onelink.me/e76N/782c66a8\"><i>Download The Post\u2019s app</i></a><i> and turn on alert notifications for The 7 or </i><a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/newsletters/the-7/?method=SURL&location=ART&initiative=THE7FOOTER\"><i>sign up for the newsletter</i></a><i>.</i>",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
